{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791193964,"nonce":"8wH9k9TBcs1q4hhue5Bk80u9JyM=","message":"Fixed in blinc_gpu, and the defect is wider than first reported.\n\n\nBC3's alpha block is a BC4 block. Measured through Blinc's own encode_bc3 path\nwith the same method: tbc 42.56dB against 69.05dB for the nearest palette\nentry on tbc's own alpha endpoints, the identical 26.49dB gap as BC4. So this\nwas never only the game kit. Blinc's own 2D image cache, which picks BC3 for\nany image with meaningful alpha, was losing the same quality on every\ntransparent image and mask.\n\n\nblinc_gpu::bc_encode keeps tbc's endpoints and replaces each pixel's 3-bit\nindex with the nearest of the eight palette values. One pure function,\nrepick_block, applied to the right bytes: BC4 is one plane, BC3's alpha is the\nfirst eight bytes of each sixteen, and BC5 is two planes. The colour half of a\nBC3 block is not touched, and a test asserts it is byte-identical to tbc's.\n\nencode_bc4_red and encode_bc5_rg are new public functions with the same\nsignatures as the game kit's private copies, so the kit can delegate to them.\n\n\n- Smooth gradient: BC4 and BC3 alpha 42.56dB -\u003e 69.05dB, exactly the ceiling\n  for their endpoints.\n- Noise with hard edges: BC4 24.22dB -\u003e 44.70dB, about +20.5dB, matching\n  ashui's +21dB on a real 2K texture. Not specific to smooth data.\n- Dimensions that are not multiples of four encode and give the right length.\n\ntests/bc4_quality.rs now has live guards through the public API (within a\ndecibel of the best possible for the endpoints, and never worse than raw tbc),\nand keeps the raw-tbc tests as #[ignore]d canaries. When a canary passes, tbc\nhas been fixed and the correction can be deleted.\n\n\npackages/blinc_game_kit is its own repo (project-blinc/blinc_game_kit), tracked\nby neither this repo nor the workspace, and pinned to a Blinc rev. Its\nbc_encode.rs encode_bc4_red and encode_bc5_rg should call\nblinc_gpu::bc_encode instead of tbc directly, and its pin needs bumping. That\nis a separate repository's commit and push, so it has not been touched.","files":null}]}